        "problem": "Find ${\u22c2}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}$, given that $I={2,4,5},$ and\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{X}_{i}={i,\\,i+1,\u2026,6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
        "worked_solution": "The intersection of a family of indexed sets ${{A}_{i}}_{i\\in I}$ contains all elements that belong to *all* sets in our family:\n\n$$\n{\u22c2}_{i\\in I}{A}_{i}={x\\in U\\,:\\,x\\in {A}_{i}\\,\\,\\text{for all\u00a0}{A}_{i},\\,\\,i\\in I}\n$$\n\nwhere $U$ is a universal set.\n\nTherefore, in our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\u22c2}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i} & ={X}_{2}\\cap {X}_{4}\\cap {X}_{5} \\\\  & ={2,3,4,5,6}\\,\\cap \\,{4,5,6}\\,\\cap \\,{5,6} \\\\  & ={5,6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
